[
  {
    "uid": "C0169",
    "text": "What gives a category its meaning?\nHow do classifications shape people's lives?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2458,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "categories-session-2",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0170",
    "text": "It is evening. The worktable is cleared for a new session. Compare categories defined by relationships with classifications used in institutions. Consider how those practices shape conduct.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2459,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "categories-session-2",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2460,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "categories-session-2",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0171",
    "text": "Does this argument contradict its own example?\nCan limited viewpoints still be checked?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2461,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "categories-session-3",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0172",
    "text": "The next morning, we return to a cleared worktable. Examine a critic's conflicting claims about originals and copies. Then compare the limits of an observer's viewpoint with the possibility of independent checks.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2462,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "categories-session-3",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2463,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "categories-session-3",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0173",
    "text": "Do genes determine a whole life?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2464,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "planet",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0174",
    "text": "This comparison covers c. 1900\u20132020. Distinct inherited factors and DNA address the earlier problem of heredity. Development and environment still matter; genes are not a complete prediction of an organism's life.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2465,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "planet",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2466,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "planet",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0175",
    "text": "How does industry change the climate?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2467,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "planet-session-2",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0176",
    "text": "It is evening. The worktable is cleared for a new session. Connect fossil-fuel emissions with the way greenhouse gases affect heat loss. Compare that explanation with records of global warming.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2468,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "planet-session-2",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2469,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "planet-session-2",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0177",
    "text": "What can old air tell us?\nWhere did the extra lead come from?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2470,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "planet-session-3",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0178",
    "text": "The next morning, we return to a cleared worktable. Old air bubbles preserve atmospheric history. Lead contamination in dating work also becomes evidence about modern pollution; these records answer different questions.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2471,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "planet-session-3",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2472,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "planet-session-3",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0179",
    "text": "Does geography decide history?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2473,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "planet-session-4",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0180",
    "text": "Later that day, the worktable is ready for another session. Connect organisms through food webs and revisit the history of forced labour in trade. Geography and ecology affect human choices without determining them.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2474,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "planet-session-4",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2475,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "planet-session-4",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0181",
    "text": "What if the model meets an unfamiliar case?\nWhat would make this finding more convincing?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2476,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "future-laboratory",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0182",
    "text": "Imagine a remote observatory. Compare a model's predictions with a proposed trial, an unfamiliar case and readings from separate instruments.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2477,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "future-laboratory",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2479,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "future-laboratory",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0183",
    "text": "Imagine an observatory far from Earth. It needs ways to check its findings and decide what it may do before a reply arrives.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2478,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "skip bridge",
        "owner": "future-laboratory",
        "field": "onAlreadyComplete.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0184",
    "text": "Can others check the distant finding?\nWhen should the local system stop and ask?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2480,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "future-laboratory-session-2",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0185",
    "text": "It is evening. The worktable is cleared for a new session. The remote observatory needs authority limits while Earth is out of contact. Keep records of how findings were made and protect their transmission, while keeping their limits visible.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2481,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "future-laboratory-session-2",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2482,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "future-laboratory-session-2",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0186",
    "text": "Who will do the necessary care?\nMust everyone want the same good life?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2483,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "future-commons",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0187",
    "text": "These imagined workshops apply earlier arguments about useful work and control. Machinery can save effort while care and other demanding work still need to be shared.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2484,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "future-commons",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2486,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "future-commons",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0188",
    "text": "People can challenge and revise the community's shared rules. They still need to organize care, divide work fairly and make room for different ways of living.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2485,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "completion/ending",
        "owner": "future-commons",
        "field": "completionText"
      },
      {
        "row": 2492,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "completion/ending",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-3",
        "field": "completionText"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0189",
    "text": "Who can challenge a rapid decision?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2487,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-2",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0190",
    "text": "It is evening. The worktable is cleared for a new session. A city's quick response meets residents' conflicting priorities. Provide a way to inspect and challenge decisions while acknowledging the cost of delay.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2488,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-2",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2489,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-2",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0191",
    "text": "How can we keep shared rules open to change?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2490,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-3",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0192",
    "text": "The next morning, we return to a cleared worktable. How can people affected by shared resources challenge and revise the rules? Care, fair work and disagreement still need attention.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2491,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-3",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2493,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-3",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0193",
    "text": "An editor compares manuscripts and shows uncertain readings. Readers can judge the choices instead of receiving an unexplained final version.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2494,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "milestone-critical-edition",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0194",
    "text": "An edition that shows its doubts",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2495,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "milestone-critical-edition",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0195",
    "text": "Venus is observed in both crescent and nearly full phases. That range conflicts with the standard Ptolemaic arrangement of Venus. It rules out that arrangement, not every model in which Earth stays still.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2496,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "milestone-strict-ptolemy-challenged",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0196",
    "text": "Strict Ptolemaic Venus is challenged",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2497,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "milestone-strict-ptolemy-challenged",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0197",
    "text": "Knowing which events came first does not tell us how many years separated them. Rock order and numerical age are different questions.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2498,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "milestone-age-still-open",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0198",
    "text": "Sequence is not duration",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2499,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "milestone-age-still-open",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0199",
    "text": "Similarities among living things can reflect shared ancestry. Their history branches rather than forming a ladder with humans as its required top.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2500,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "milestone-branching-descent",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0200",
    "text": "Resemblance can record shared descent",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2501,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "milestone-branching-descent",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0201",
    "text": "Earth formed about 4.54 billion years ago. The estimate draws on radioactive dating and evidence from the early solar system, not the order of rock layers alone.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2502,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "milestone-earth-age-measured",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0202",
    "text": "Earth is about 4.54 billion years old",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2503,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "milestone-earth-age-measured",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0203",
    "text": "Lead in blank laboratory tests reveals contamination that interferes with dating ancient material. Comparing older and modern environments turns that measurement problem into evidence of industrial lead pollution.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2504,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "milestone-industrial-lead-footprint",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0204",
    "text": "An analytical nuisance exposes industrial pollution",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2505,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "milestone-industrial-lead-footprint",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0205",
    "text": "People can challenge and revise the community's shared rules. They still disagree about how to divide work, provide care and prevent people from being forced into decisions.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2506,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "milestone-unfinished-common-world",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0206",
    "text": "A shared world with obligations still disputed",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2507,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "milestone-unfinished-common-world",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0207",
    "text": "The archive records what people saw and marks the nights when they could not observe. Missing evidence is not treated as evidence that nothing happened.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2508,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-sky-archive",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0208",
    "text": "A sky archive with its gaps",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2509,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-sky-archive",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0209",
    "text": "Eclipses recur in patterns. Those patterns help predict when to watch, but not every eclipse is visible from every place.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2510,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-eclipse-pattern",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0210",
    "text": "Recurring eclipse seasons",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2511,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-eclipse-pattern",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0211",
    "text": "The records suggest when an eclipse may occur. Plan a watch, but clouds or your location may prevent you from seeing one.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2512,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-watch-window",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0212",
    "text": "A watch, not a promised eclipse",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2513,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-watch-window",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0213",
    "text": "People can predict an eclipse and still give it a religious or political meaning. Prediction does not automatically replace those beliefs.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2514,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-portent-and-pattern",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0214",
    "text": "Prediction alongside portent",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2515,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-portent-and-pattern",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0215",
    "text": "A calendar connects the seasons with farming and food storage. It helps people prepare before the next flood or harvest.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2516,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-seasonal-calendar",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0216",
    "text": "A calendar for fields and stores",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2517,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-seasonal-calendar",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0217",
    "text": "Agreed dates let a community organize work and festivals together. People can share a calendar without agreeing about the nature of the universe.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2518,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-shared-year",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0218",
    "text": "A publicly shared year",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2519,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-shared-year",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0219",
    "text": "Earth's shadow explains why the Moon darkens during a lunar eclipse. This connects a repeated observation with a physical cause.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2520,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-natural-eclipse",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0220",
    "text": "An eclipse has a natural cause",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2521,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-natural-eclipse",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0221",
    "text": "An explanation should say when it applies. A lunar eclipse requires Earth to block the sunlight that would otherwise reach the Moon.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2522,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-conditional-cause",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0222",
    "text": "An explanation tied to conditions",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2523,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-conditional-cause",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0223",
    "text": "A proposed rule says justice means returning what you owe. But returning a weapon to someone who may harm others would cause harm. This example shows why repayment alone cannot define justice.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2524,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-debt-objection",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0224",
    "text": "Repayment can do harm",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2525,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-debt-objection",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0225",
    "text": "The rule that justice means repaying debts fails when returning a weapon could cause harm. Finding that problem gives a reason to keep questioning the definition; it does not yet supply a complete new one.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2526,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-examined-definition",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0226",
    "text": "A definition still under examination",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2527,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-examined-definition",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0227",
    "text": "An examined life means questioning how you live and why. The aim is to judge your choices, not simply accept praise or custom.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2528,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-examined-life",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0228",
    "text": "The examined life",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2529,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-examined-life",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0229",
    "text": "Explaining how an eclipse happens does not settle what it means to a community. This comparison separates a physical cause from a religious or social interpretation.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2530,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cause-and-meaning",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0230",
    "text": "Cause need not erase meaning",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2531,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cause-and-meaning",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0231",
    "text": "A claim should be open to questions and difficult examples. The standing of the person making it is not enough to settle whether it is right.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2532,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-answerable-claims",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0232",
    "text": "Claims answerable to objections",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2533,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-answerable-claims",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0233",
    "text": "Plato proposes unchanging Forms, such as Beauty itself, to explain what changing examples share. The beautiful things we encounter are imperfect and changeable, unlike the Form he describes.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2534,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-stable-forms",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0234",
    "text": "Plato: stable Forms",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2535,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-stable-forms",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0235",
    "text": "Aristotle places form in the particular thing: what makes this living thing the kind of thing it is. This differs from Plato's separate Forms.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2536,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-form-in-particular",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0236",
    "text": "Aristotle: form in the particular",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2537,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-form-in-particular",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0237",
    "text": "Comparing animals' parts and activities gives a basis for grouping them. One shared feature alone may not be enough to establish a group.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2538,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-animal-kinds",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0238",
    "text": "Animals compared by structures and activities",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2539,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-animal-kinds",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0239",
    "text": "Aristotle understands an animal's parts through the organization of the whole animal. An organ is not explained only by listing its material: its role in that living animal also matters.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2540,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-part-and-function",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0240",
    "text": "An organ understood through the whole animal",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2541,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-part-and-function",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0241",
    "text": "Aristotle distinguishes four kinds of explanation: what something is made of, its form, what produces it, and its purpose. One answer need not replace the others.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2542,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-four-causes",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0242",
    "text": "Different questions about why",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2543,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-four-causes",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0243",
    "text": "A valid argument has a conclusion that must follow if its starting claims are true. It still matters whether those claims are actually true.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2544,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-valid-inference",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0244",
    "text": "A conclusion follows from premises",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2545,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-valid-inference",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0245",
    "text": "An argument can follow the rules of logic and still start from a false claim. Check both the reasoning and its starting claims.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2546,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-valid-not-true",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0246",
    "text": "Validity is not truth",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2547,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-valid-not-true",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0247",
    "text": "For Aristotle, living well requires habits and practical judgment developed through action. Knowing a rule is not the same as being able to act well.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2548,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cultivated-virtue",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0248",
    "text": "Virtue as cultivated judgment",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2549,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cultivated-virtue",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0249",
    "text": "In Plato's cave story, a prisoner learns that familiar shadows are not the whole world. Education means reconsidering what he takes for reality, not simply receiving more facts about the shadows.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2550,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-turning-attention",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0250",
    "text": "Education as a turning of attention",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2551,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-turning-attention",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0251",
    "text": "Stories about Diogenes contrast his few wants with a ruler's offer of wealth. Needing less can make it harder for a powerful patron to buy someone's loyalty. This ideal does not mean that forced poverty is harmless.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2552,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cynic-sufficiency",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0252",
    "text": "Freedom by needing less",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2553,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cynic-sufficiency",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0253",
    "text": "Cities disagree about what counts as respectable. A custom's local popularity therefore cannot, by itself, settle whether it is a good way to live.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2554,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-convention-questioned",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0254",
    "text": "Local respectability does not settle a good life",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2555,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-convention-questioned",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0255",
    "text": "Stoic practice focuses effort on judgments and responses rather than things we cannot control. It does not deny the pain of loss or injustice.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2556,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-stoic-control",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0256",
    "text": "Care for the judgment that is yours",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2557,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-stoic-control",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0257",
    "text": "Stoic thinkers connect care for one's own judgments with concern for other people who share in reason. Their idea of fellowship can extend beyond the boundaries of a single city.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2558,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cosmopolis",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0258",
    "text": "Fellowship beyond one city",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2559,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-cosmopolis",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0259",
    "text": "Epicurus argues that there is no suffering after death because there is no remaining sensation. The argument offers relief from fear without denying grief or ending disagreement.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2560,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-release-from-terror",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0260",
    "text": "Freedom from the terror of death",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2561,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-release-from-terror",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0261",
    "text": "Epicurus places friendship, security and simple enjoyment at the centre of a good life. Seeking pleasure in this account does not mean endlessly increasing wealth or indulgence.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2562,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-garden-pleasure",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0262",
    "text": "Pleasure in friendship and sufficiency",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2563,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-garden-pleasure",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0263",
    "text": "When the available accounts conflict and neither settles the question, a skeptic can withhold agreement. Leaving judgment open is different from proving that both sides are false or that knowledge is impossible.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2564,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-suspended-assent",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  }
]